UPPLY

I write to give notice of a further Delay Event under clause 9.2.

Clause 6.4 of the Amended and Restated Agreement required Brisamar to provide=
 and energise a permanent 400A three-phase supply to the installation hall di=
stribution board not later than 7 February 2025. As of today, 9 March 2025, t=
he supply is not available. The controls cabinets for Bays 1 and 2 are instal=
led and loop checks were programmed to start tomorrow, 10 March 2025. Under c=
lause 8.5 testing and commissioning cannot commence until the permanent suppl=
y is energised.

Delay Event: failure to comply with clause 6.4 (clause 9.1(b)).

Likely effect: the loop-check, software-load and dry-run sequence cannot star=
t. Every day without the supply from 10 March is a day of critical delay to P=
ractical Completion. Taking Marc's latest indication of the week of 17 March,=
 we estimate 21 days.

Extension of time claimed: 21 days to Practical Completion, in addition to th=
e 14 days claimed in my notice of 21 February 2025 in respect of the Bay 3 sl=
ab.

On the slab: we have not received the main contractor's survey referred to in=
 your e-mail of 24 February. We maintain that the slab is Brisamar's responsi=
bility under clause 6.2. We have continued installation outside zone C4=E2=80=
=93C7 as you requested, but we cannot set the supports in that zone, and CO-3=
 remains unsigned. Unless we receive an instruction by Friday 14 March we wil=
l have to suspend work on conveyor line 2 in that zone.

Kind regards,

Priya Nair
Project Manager, Tidewell Fabrication Ltd


